The page's run: 200 agents, tolerance 0.05, 100 ticks

tick      clumps   mean gap      settled
0              1     0.0027         1.00
1              1     0.0027         1.00
10             1     0.0027         1.00
100            1     0.0027         1.00

Nothing moves. 200 agents on the unit interval sit 0.003 apart on
average, so every agent is already inside its neighbour's tolerance and
the jump rule never fires. The mechanism needs a sparse population.

Population sweep, 100 ticks each

n       clumps 0    clumps   settled 0     settled
10             4         3        0.90        1.00
20             7         4        0.85        1.00
40             5         4        0.97        1.00
80             3         3        1.00        1.00
200            1         1        1.00        1.00

At n = 10 the model does what it is meant to: 4 scattered opinions
condense into 3 clumps and every agent ends within 0.05 of a neighbour.
